## Decision

Proceed only as a small efficiency/validity diagnostic. Sequential validation of paired cost differences is mathematically sound under explicit sampling and multiplicity conditions, but its central ingredients already exist. Comparing sample medians cannot by itself certify an all-center stable coreset or near-optimality. The remaining useful question is whether a valid, batched validator produces a useful runtime–quality tradeoff for continuous-coordinate medians after paying for candidate construction, validation and fallback. Novelty is not established.

